# Line-ending policy — study 05 (external cache throughput and consistency)
#
# A generated report carries an "inputs digest": a content hash over the bytes of
# every result file in the run. Git's line-ending conversion rewrites those bytes
# on checkout, so the same measurements hash differently after a clone, a new
# worktree or a branch switch. That is not hypothetical in this repository: study
# 03's matrix hashed two different ways and the fix was to pin the affected trees
# to LF.
#
# This file is deliberately scoped to study 05. The root .gitattributes covers
# studies 02 and 03, study 01 pins its own tree, and study 04 has its own scoped
# file; a study-scoped file keeps this study's merge surface small while more than
# one agent is working in the repository.

# Provenance: these bytes are hashed, so they are pinned.
results/**           text eol=lf
reports/**           text eol=lf

# Everything executable or readable as documentation.
*.sh                 text eol=lf
*.go                 text eol=lf
*.sql                text eol=lf
*.md                 text eol=lf
*.puml               text eol=lf
*.yml                text eol=lf
*.yaml               text eol=lf
*.env                text eol=lf
go.mod               text eol=lf
go.sum               text eol=lf
Containerfile        text eol=lf

# Diagrams are rendered output.
rendered/*.svg       text eol=lf
